{{also|Bonk}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Of {{onomatopoeic|en|title=imitative}} origin. Compare {{noncog|en|bang}}, {{m|en|bounce}}, {{m|en|bump}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-bonk.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/bɒŋk/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/bɑŋk/|/bɔŋk/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒŋk|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} To [[strike]] or [[collide]] with something.
# {{lb|en|informal|chiefly|UK|ambitransitive}} To have [[sexual intercourse]] (with).
#: {{syn|en|boink|discuss Uganda|have sex|Thesaurus:copulate|Thesaurus:copulate with}}
#* {{quote-av|en|author=w:Mike Leigh|year=1993|title=Naked|passage=Sophie (Katrin Cartlidge) What is a proper relationship? / Louise (Lesley Sharp): Living with someone who talks to you after they've '''bonked''' ya.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|writer={{w|Richard Curtis}}|title={{w|Four Weddings and a Funeral}}|year=1994|role=Scarlett|actor=Charlotte Coleman|passage=Because most of the blokes I fancy think l'm stupid and pointless—and, so, they just '''bonk''' me and then leave me. And the kind of blokes that do fancy me, I think are drips. I can't even be bothered to '''bonk''' them. Which does sort of leave me a bit nowhere.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theguardian.com/politics/commentisfree/2022/oct/10/the-tory-ministers-bonking-for-britain-idea-is-a-vile-vision-lurking-behind-cheeky-carry-on-imagery|title=The Tory minister’s ‘bonking for Britain’ idea is a vile vision lurking behind cheeky Carry On imagery|date=2022-10-10|work=The Guardian|author=Zoe Williams|passage=But let’s not kid ourselves about '''bonking''' for Britain: this is just “the great replacement theory” with a tax code.}}
# {{lb|en|skateboarding|snowboarding}} To hit something with the front of the board, especially in midair.
# {{lb|en|informal|sports}} To experience sudden and severe [[fatigue]] in an endurance sports event due to [[glycogen]] depletion.
#: {{syn|en|hit the wall}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|title=Raising the Bar|page=29|author=Gary Erickson; Lois Ann Lorentzen|publisher=Jossey-Bass|isbn=978-0-7879-8671-1|passage=I had eaten five of my six PowerBars.  I was exhausted and famished. In cycling they describe what was happening to me as '''''bonking''''': my body was out of fuel and had no more energy.}}

